WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.654
Three failures. One question: what can the evidence prove?

2
00:00:04.654 --> 00:00:13.813
01 / The response is lost. The client retries with the same idempotency key.

3
00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:16.860
Several requests can still represent a single business operation.

4
00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:21.414
The recorded result: one transfer, one reservation, one settlement.

5
00:00:21.414 --> 00:00:29.458
02 / Duplicate and older webhooks arrive. They must not repeat the financial effect.

6
00:00:29.458 --> 00:00:34.516
The journal preserves one settlement. Duplicate notifications remain inspectable.

7
00:00:34.516 --> 00:00:39.532
03 / The provider accepted the request, but the application has no usable response.

8
00:00:39.532 --> 00:00:45.090
Unknown is not rejected. Funds stay reserved; a timeout does not release them.

9
00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:49.110
A later authoritative observation resolves the transfer with one settlement.

10
00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:54.615
Actual Claude Code output, recorded separately while the outcome was still unknown.

11
00:00:54.615 --> 00:00:59.647
Claude called three read-only MCP tools: trace, invariants and exceptions.

12
00:00:59.647 --> 00:01:05.659
Its report separates the local reservation from the unknown external outcome.

13
00:01:05.659 --> 00:01:10.174
15 evidence IDs cited. All were present in tool output. No mutating tool calls.

14
00:01:10.174 --> 00:01:16.000
Explore the replay, inspect the code, or reproduce the scenarios locally.
